# T-152-004 Execution Plan

## Scope
- Read-only audit of 10+ CLI commands: recall, remember, memory subcommands, checkpoint, run
- Write: docs/audits/sprint-152/T-152-004-cli-memory-checkpoint.md

## Approach
1. Confirm dist/cli/entry.js exists, invoke `--help` for each target command
2. Dry-run reads only — no `remember` writes, no `memory rebuild` actual rebuild
3. Exercise FTS5 dual-layer recall with TR + EN + DE query terms
4. Verify Memory V2 DB-first integration (.brain/memory.db exists, queryable via recall)
5. Document findings in structured report
6. Write .result with selfAssessment

## Commands To Smoke
- `deckent recall "docker heartbeat"` — EN
- `deckent recall "adr governance"` — EN (hybrid)
- `deckent recall "adr yönetişim"` — TR (if DB has entries)
- `deckent recall "architekturentscheidung"` — DE (fallback test)
- `deckent remember --help`
- `deckent memory --help`
- `deckent memory rebuild --help` (avoid actual rebuild)
- `deckent memory export --help`
- `deckent memory stats`
- `deckent memory-query` (check if exists)
- `deckent checkpoint --help`
- `deckent checkpoint list`
- `deckent run --help`

## Report Structure
Follow directive's mandated template:
- Özet
- Bulgular [PASS|FAIL|REGRESSION|MISSING|DRIFT]
